After the edit:
1. Validate JSON: `node -e "JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('C:/Users/wompu/.claude/settings.json'))"`
2. Verify mirror sync: hash of C: should equal H: (the c-to-h-mirror PostToolUse hook fires on the Edit; if not, manually `cp C:/Users/wompu/.claude/settings.json H:/.claude/settings.json`).

## What this hook does

`H:/prism/.claude/hooks/settings-mirror-guard.mjs` (already on disk, committed):

- Runs at every SessionStart (after `session-id-pin`, before any hook that reads settings).
- Hashes both layers; exits silently if equal.
- If drift detected:
  - Always reconciles C: → H: (canonical direction per CLAUDE.md).
  - If H: was newer (someone edited H: directly against doctrine) → emits a LOUD warning so the user knows their H: edits got overwritten.
  - If C: was newer (external script bypassed c-to-h-mirror) → quiet sync, log only.
- Logs every reconciliation to `state/shared/settings-mirror-guard.log` (JSONL).
- Always non-blocking; emits `{continue:true}`.

## Rollback

`PRISM_MIRROR_GUARD_OFF=1` in env disables the guard.

